settings-paper-engine-card = Engine
settings-paper-engine-card-desc = Choose which program displays images. Videos and Wallpaper Engine scenes always use the built-in renderer.
settings-paper-engine-label = Wallpaper engine
settings-paper-engine-desc = I prefer Skwd-paper because I made it, but use Awww if that's your thing :)
settings-paper-static-backend-label = Static wallpaper backend
settings-paper-performance-card = Performance
settings-paper-performance-card-desc = Cut VRAM, RAM, and GPU use by dropping transitions and using the direct video path. Applies with the next wallpaper.
settings-paper-multi-process-label = Shared video process
settings-paper-multi-process-desc = Run all video wallpapers in one renderer and Vulkan device. Identical videos share decoding. Disable only for troubleshooting.
settings-paper-performance-mode-label = Performance mode
settings-paper-performance-mode-desc = Changes become hard cuts. Cover-fill video walls hand decoded NV12 frames straight to the compositor, saving roughly 45% of video VRAM. Fit and centre keep the standard renderer.
settings-paper-idle-pause-label = Idle pause
settings-paper-idle-pause-desc = Pause video decode and audio after this many seconds without input (0 disables). Resumes instantly on activity.
settings-paper-fill-mode-label = Fill mode
settings-paper-fill-mode-desc = How the wallpaper is fitted to the screen. Applies to images and videos.
